    {
      "path": "internal/ledger/ledger.go",
      "summary": "Keeps the pass rules shared with --continue history and drops the single-file store.",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "newRange": [
            67,
            81
          ],
          "summary": "fresh owns the date rules: unreadable, dated in the future, or 7 days old or older.",
          "rationale": "Both Proves (instance history) and the shared store call fresh, so one owner decides expiry. A future date is refused because a forged young date would otherwise outlive the 7-day limit.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-shared-ledger"
        },
        {
          "oldRange": [
            159,
            231
          ],
          "summary": "The single ledger.json store with its lock is removed in favor of store.go.",
          "rationale": "docs/ledger-placement.md measured that one shared file keeps one entry per step, so two branches overwrite each other's passes even under the lock. The directory store keeps every pass side by side.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-shared-ledger"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "internal/ledger/store.go",
      "summary": "New directory ledger: one immutable file per pass named by stamp and content digest, plus a copy of its evidence.",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "newRange": [
            103,
            158
          ],
          "summary": "find opens only the passes whose name carries the current stamp, and reads other passes only to explain what changed.",
          "rationale": "The first version read every pass in a slot, so plan time grew with history. With the stamp filter, plan took 8, 10 and 27 ms with 0, 1,000 and 10,000 other passes (docs/ledger-placement.md). The newest standing pass wins; when none stands, the newest refused pass gives the reason.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-shared-ledger"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            253,
            296
          ],
          "summary": "add refuses a non-green, unstamped, unowned or wrong-claim-version result and evidence that misses the contract, then copies evidence and publishes the pass.",
          "rationale": "The reader repeats every check, because another writer of the ledger can bypass add. Evidence is copied before the pass file appears, so a reader never sees a pass without evidence. Proven by TestRecordRefusesWhatMayNotBecomeAPass and ledger.md refusal steps (session TRsE8o). A consistent forgery by someone with write access still stands, as the placement doc states.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-shared-ledger"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            307,
            328
          ],
          "summary": "prune removes a written slot's passes 7 days old or older, then their evidence, and leaves damaged files alone.",
          "rationale": "Only slots a run writes are pruned, so recording stays cheap. A reader racing a prune finds the pass gone and runs live, which is the safe side. Proven by the expired-pass test in plan_test.go and ledger.md age-out step.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-shared-ledger"
        }
      ]
    },
